/-!
# Actual constant terms and comparisons for the cusp normalization

The constant additive complex sheaf on the actual central fibre, its
normalization pushforward, and the three actual curve pushforwards have
canonical injective maps to the corresponding actual holomorphic terms.
The first pullback, both source-oriented curve lifts, and their signed
difference form commuting squares with these termwise inclusions.

All constant sheaves are the proved sheafified constant sheaves, not
globally constant function presheaves. Their actual stalks are identified
with `ℂ`, compatibly with literal constant representatives. Finite
biproducts, final endpoint maps, and exactness are handled separately.
-/
